            "review_title": "Review at Nathalie's Thai Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Traveler of the Wild\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam66 contributions\n0\nGreat Vietnamese Thai restaurant, not authentic, but still pretty good! (Thais don't use chopsticks:)\nFeb 2025 • Family\nA very solid and mid-priced attempt at a Thai restaurant in District 7. Food fresh and well served but definitely 'localised' (i.e Less spicy, sweeter) and including some inauthentic 'Thai' dishes. I would love to see Nathalie's waitstaff give the option for customers to have 'Thai style' (i.e More authentically cooked) like Golden Elephant and Bangkok Kitchen offer. Also, a sure sign that this place is not authentic Thai is the sight of chopsticks on the table. Thai's do not use chopsticks traditionally- they eat with a fork and spoon. Also, no acknowledgement of HM The King and HM The Queen- a sure sign that the place is not Thai run. However, the food was tasty and hot and quickly served the waitstaff friendly and accommodating. I just wish they would honour the food with more authentic Thai style and also make it feel Thai inside (play Thai music, honour the Royal family) and also have a wider selection of Thai beers on draft (Singha, Chang Draught) as well as Thai Whisky served by the table with mixers as is common in Thailand. Definitely worth a visit but expect Vietnamese Thai rather than real Thai.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nLovely attempt at Thai food and quick friendly service but look a little beneath the surface and it's pure Vietnamese Thai (not authentic).\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten February 2, 2025",
